@@ -6,7 +6,7 @@ In-memory inventory service. `api.handle(request)` maps a request
 
 ## Endpoints
 
-- `GET /items` → `{"items": [...]}`: every item, ordered by `id`.
+- `GET /items?limit=<1..100>&cursor=<opaque>` → `{"items": [...], "next_cursor": ...}`: items ordered by `id` (default limit 20). Follow `next_cursor` on the next request; it is null on the last page. Invalid limits or cursors return 400 with `{"error": "..."}`.
 - `GET /items/<id>` → the item, 404 when unknown, 400 when `id` is not a number.
 
 Run the tests with `python3 -m unittest`.
